ived_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"content_type":"application/json","state":"uploaded","size":653,"digest":"sha256:b69ae42a31581039291b4b6929d7b8d4f842f0b5e285ad8336e1266f0a65ef7c","download_count":0,"created_at":"2026-11-19T17:06:26Z","updated_at":"2026-11-19T17:06:26Z","browser_download_url":"https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/releases/download/m142-v0.14.2/m14stage2-starter-manifest.json"}],"tarball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enginsoysal/engacer-os/tarball/m142-v0.14.2","zipball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enginsoysal/engacer-os/zipball/m142-v0.14.2","body":"# Engacer OS M14.2 / 0.14.2 - Native Windows execution lifetime\n\nDevelopment media passes **M14-STAGE2-VM-v1** native qualification. Actual website publication is being verified. Read the bounded scope below before testing.\n\nThis stage implements private Windows process address spaces, preemptive threads, static/dynamic TLS, shared events/semaphores/timers and the documented AMD64 hardware-fault and C exception/unwind profile. Application instructions execute through Engacer OS's own kernel and compatibility APIs. QEMU and VMware are external test hosts; an embedded Windows guest is not the implementation.\n\nBuild: `6e242c9d2f8b626e96a952a39d50fe49`, binding 626 compiled source inputs.\n\n- ISO SHA-256: `b02decae4177bc707554c610a355931ed4246142638ac8b57e4e9550de7cde08`\n- VMware ZIP SHA-256: `b24eb8a175f2e1f5b6af9a0a1ba44c4900ab1c1c11faa26e04bb91d944d3029b`\n\nThe prepared package retains a blank growable 20-GiB SATA disk, two CPUs, 128 MiB RAM and x64 UEFI with Secure Boot disabled. Installation erases the selected disposable disk. The exact archive has passed actual headless VMware installation, restart with the ISO retained and two independent disk-only starts. Fresh compact, ordinary and actual 3840-by-2160 native profiles also pass installation and independent startup. These named virtual profiles do not establish universal hardware compatibility.\n\nThe original supported 7-Zip console/MSI lifecycle verifies all 106 original payload hashes. Two unmodified original 7-Zip children can create separate archives concurrently. Original Notepad++ and SumatraPDF images remain inspection-only. Firefox is a verified optional installer download; installation and execution are unavailable. Original Windows GUI support and reusable arbitrary MSI services are later stages.\n\nTwenty repeated task closes retain zero managed pages after one-time initialization. Thread and four-process cancellation pass 21 repetitions: four first-run transition pages, then zero retained pages, with both configured CPUs halted while blocked. The four-process cancellation profile peaks at 633 protected group-owned pages; this is not total OS memory. Malformed unwind/context cases remain contained with a responsive desktop. The real Firefox transfer is cancelled safely, then completed and independently SHA-256 checked. [Exact-source native acceptance](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/6a449080c78fb4ff90050ec9bd0e97d521e63543/evidence/M14/2/acceptance-results.json), [resource accounting](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/6a449080c78fb4ff90050ec9bd0e97d521e63543/evidence/M14/2/resources.json).\n\nThe first profile bounds live Windows processes to four and threads to sixteen per process. It retains the 10,000-owned-page and 128-MiB virtual process limits, 32 modules and 32-MiB mapped image limit. Shared synchronization is bounded to 128 objects, 32 created objects per process, 64 grants per process and 32 handles per wait. Idle registries allocate no data pages. Root metadata omits the private child-output tail, saving four pages compared with the full child slab. These are component and ownership bounds, not total OS consumption or a faster-than-Windows claim.\n\nSupported C handlers, selected version-1 unwind operations and checked nested hardware-fault continuation are distinct from general C++ runtime support. Custom security/environment inheritance, arbitrary handle inheritance, Windows SMP, mutexes, APCs, dynamic function tables, unsupported unwind forms and general Windows application compatibility remain unavailable. Unsupported operations must fail clearly. See the [runtime contract](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/6a449080c78fb4ff90050ec9bd0e97d521e63543/docs/architecture/runtime-m142.md), [child ownership](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/6a449080c78fb4ff90050ec9bd0e97d521e63543/docs/architecture/children-m142.md), [synchronization limits](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/6a449080c78fb4ff90050ec9bd0e97d521e63543/docs/architecture/synchronization-m142.md) and [exception scope](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/6a449080c78fb4ff90050ec9bd0e97d521e63543/docs/architecture/exceptions-m142.md).\n\n[Installation](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/6a449080c78fb4ff90050ec9bd0e97d521e63543/docs/handbook/install-m142.md), [first day](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/6a449080c78fb4ff90050ec9bd0e97d521e63543/docs/handbook/first-day-m142.md), [Windows tasks and browser downloads](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/6a449080c78fb4ff90050ec9bd0e97d521e63543/docs/handbook/windows-m142.md), [stage progress](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/6a449080c78fb4ff90050ec9bd0e97d521e63543/docs/milestones/m14-2.md). M14.15 remains the mandatory whole-system CPU/RAM/storage optimization gate. Windows x86 is M15 and Win16/DOS is M16. No new long-duration stability, GPU gaming or universal hardware qualification is claimed.\n\nUse the matching [prepared VMware ZIP](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/releases/download/m142-v0.14.2/EngacerOS-M14STAGE2-VMware.zip), [ISO](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/releases/download/m142-v0.14.2/EngacerOS-M14STAGE2.iso) and [complete checksums](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/releases/download/m142-v0.14.2/M14STAGE2-SHA256SUMS.txt).\n"}